  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdd `research/p104-pooled-collectors/`, an exact dirty-restored three-target correction that pools the `{0,2}` and `{0,1,2}` incidence groups.\n\n```diff\n- PR2504: 92 new helpers, 517 ADDs, 283 transports, rank mass 828\n+ pooled: 91 new helpers, 514 ADDs, 280 transports, rank mass 819\n```\n\nThe local profile loses exactly `H1 + H2 + H6`, with no rank increases. The complete word has 4852 events and 371 independent inputs. Y0/Y1/Y2 become identity transfers; the other 101 targets retain their original G/2 updates. All arbitrary dirty helper values restore. Unaffected insertions, including the late-exclusive branch, are compared literally at their original cuts.\n\nCard `p104-side-correction`, priority revision 4, refined to the explicit cross-group collector handoff. This changes the incidence-separation premise of #2460 rather than contradicting its restricted lower bound. Scientific base is `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`.\n\nCredit CubeJerry / #2504 at `9db4192bf3fd7f43c5f41ae040649067191682e0` for the 92-helper word and late-exclusive branch; ywz65 / #2460 at `a0030819c6d0e89e133cd3e52cc748035d58e3c7` for the incidence groups and mixing handoff; Ross Richardson / #2445 for two-target sharing; and the retained P104 acquisition, schedule and native-channel lineage. Exact input pins and full credit are retained in the package.\n\n[Tested artifact](https://github.com/petalas/integer-mult-bounds/tree/c7a3286860057f9240e0371b33ada37cc63b7ad7/research/p104-pooled-collectors)\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** the pinned PR2504 word uses 92 helper lifetimes, 4858 events and the larger profile above.\n  **After:** the generated pooled word uses 91 helper lifetimes and 4852 events. Sparse-rational and separate dense-quarter-integer/echelon interpreters agree on all 137641 endpoint coefficients and the exact profile deletion.\n- The registered replay passes five behavioral groups, five primary semantic faults and two independent fanout faults. Complete JSON regeneration, source/receipt failures, equivalent bases, exclusive output and optimized Git-free read-only execution are checked.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -Werror -B scripts/research_package.py \\\n  --package research/p104-pooled-collectors\n```\n\nChecked with CPython 3.12.15 on Linux x86_64 / WSL2. This is a finite logical/frame construction. Native lowering, physical source delivery, global owners and idle/residual costs, reverse admission, precision, remaining target corrections and all-size transfer are still missing. Helper lifetimes are not simultaneous stock, and boundary rank mass is not recursive excess. No unrestricted optimum, full supplier or new kappa is claimed.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** research\n\nOnly this opt-in package is added. Its predecessor circuit is retained byte-for-byte. Selected records and frozen predecessors are unchanged; this PR does not adopt the partial word into the selected supplier.\n",
